                <pb facs="0216" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/429.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Reid to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-12-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Number 334. December 2, 4 p.m. With reference to Department’s cable 2nd instant
                    re Opium Conference. British Government approves postponement. Delay caused by
                    the Foreign Office awaiting official assent of other Departments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reid.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
